<p>Australia’s most-decorated living soldier, Ben Roberts-Smith, has publicly denied five war-crime murder charges tied to deployments in Afghanistan, saying on Sunday that he is innocent and will fight the case. The 47-year-old, who was granted bail this week, is accused in the deaths of five unarmed Afghan civilians in incidents alleged to have taken place between 2009 and 2012. Each charge carries a maximum sentence of life imprisonment if he is convicted. The charges turn a long-running controversy over alleged misconduct in Afghanistan into a criminal case against a Victoria Cross recipient, bringing one of Australia’s most prominent military figures into court.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/e01qHSITNHhim9GC3e02ThH7Ahw_EyfrPu3Wj46s4BYwj7Tc3qvLK34LRgAlThkFsT6X0POnmMnWWo4CViTngUih2giJTtJ-q2VNqB1_LgcRsPTKZQs9SCmEq_FzARhq' alt='Ben Roberts-Smith departs the Federal Court in Sydney while pursuing a defamation case last year' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Unit and rank: The Week identifies Roberts-Smith as a corporal in Australia’s Special Air Service Regiment (SAS).</li><li>How the story built: Before charges were laid, war reporters had heard &quot;whispers&quot; about his conduct, and newspapers had pursued public allegations dating back to 2018.</li><li>Public symbolism: His profile reached into national ceremonial life, including a display at the Australian War Memorial and attendance at Queen Elizabeth II’s funeral in 2022.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/apr/19/australia-news-live-free-public-transport-in-victoria-extended-man-charged-with-in-nsw-ntwnfb'>Ben Roberts-Smith denies war crimes allegations – As it happened</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cy91r7ww3weo'>Australia&#x27;s most-decorated soldier vows to &#x27;fight&#x27; war crime charges</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/former-australian-soldier-speaks-out-against-allegations-afghan-war-crimes'>Former Australian soldier speaks out against allegations of Afghan war crimes</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://theweek.com/law/ben-roberts-smith-war-crimes-allegations-australia-soldier'>Ben Roberts-Smith: the allegations against Australia’s ‘uber-soldier’</a> - theweek.com</li></ul>